            <ArticleTitle>Phrenic neuropathy due to neuralgic amyotrophy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1582-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors reviewed the medical records of 33 patients diagnosed with idiopathic phrenic neuropathy and found that 17 patients had clinical features of neuralgic amyotrophy. They concluded that a careful clinical and electrodiagnostic evaluation may implicate neuralgic amyotrophy as a causative disease in patients with apparently isolated phrenic neuropathy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
